Z||000011||BigTurbo87GT||11-06-2000||11:53 AM||||Finally found info, this is copied from Word doc they sent me:<P>Fiero Turbo kit  <BR>Kit includes:<P>-Turbo AR63 trim 50 mm (300 hp)  NEW Up to 20 psi ! <BR>-Heat shield<BR>-Exhaust from original headers to turbo(Note special expansion joints) <BR>-Exhaust from turbo to tips (SPECIAL HAND MADE MUFLER)<BR>-Oil parts to turbo /From turbo <BR>-Water cooling  Inc.silicone hoses (turbo center section)<BR>-Exhaust gasket for original ”headers”(must remove ,and clean miss aligment)<BR>-Exhaust hangers <BR>-Paste for flanges <BR>-Termotec one roll<BR>-Presure pipe from comressor to int.manifold(includes injector base)<BR>-silicone hoses<BR>-Pipe clamps<BR>-Haltec F5 Extra injector drives<BR>-Injector <BR>-Oil cooler .extra flanges ,pipes,hoses and hangers <BR>-Oil Filter<BR>-K&N air filter <BR>-Spark plugs V59C<BR>-All bolts and harware <BR>-Pictures <BR>-installion instructions and tips <BR>-Tuning tips <P>Needs welding on turbo oil return line (oil pan) and exhaust hangers to Frame .<BR>All parts are JIG made <BR>No catalytic converter anymore! <P><BR>$ 3200 + Shipping ( about $300)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||jlhuber||11-06-2000||01:44 PM||||...for that price, I could stuff a lt1 or ls1 into a fiero and end up with a meaner exhaust note to boot.  course if someone wants to stick with the stock v-6 instead of a v-8 but wants more hp too, ...hey, to each his own.  thanx for the info||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||11-06-2000||04:26 PM||||Jlhuber:  If you stuff in an lt-1 for $3500 then I think you will be the first one to do so at that price.  I dont' know what archie charges for a lt-1 kit but I would think around $2000 or so for a decent kit with most of the stuff.  Then you will need all of the little extras and then actually buying the engine and engine management systems.  You could probably get a used lt-1 engine in good condition for around $1000 or maybe even more.  Junk ones will be less and will need to be rebuilt costing more money.  Have you priced an Ls-1 engine lately?  God awefully expensive.  That is around $3500 new right there.  ARchie is working on an LS1 swap right now but still isn't finished.  I think he was saying if he did all the work and supplied the kit and engine it would be around $10k or so for the swap.  Hmmm unless my math is off it seems to me $10k is more then $3500.  Do it yourself and you might be able to save around $4000 or so.  But at least you will have that really cool exhaust note!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Oh yea good info about the turbo.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000014||jlhuber||11-07-2000||12:50 PM||||I would be able to do most of the work myself.  The only thing that I would have to have custom done is the exhaust.  A friend of the family owns a massive junk yard where I am from.  They have all kinds of cars.  I haven't been there since I joined the military, but my cousin says they have a couple of fieros.  Anyway, my cousin got his friend a 350 from a wrecked state cop car for $500 and they stuffed it into his '89 trans am gta.  he has a hard time getting traction in that car now.  So I figure if I could find a motor from there (I'd even settle for another cop car motor) and buy only the parts that I cannot fabricate myself, I would hope it will be under $5000.  The statement that I made earlier about doing the ls1 thing for the same price as the turbo was just for the sake of the argument.  I know that a v8 conversion will run atleast the same amount as that turbo system.  What I was trying to point out is if I am going to spend that much on an engine mod/conversion, it will have to sound like the car has got a big pair of balls, and actually have them if someone were to call my bluff.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Standard||11-07-2000||03:19 PM||||A stock V6 sounds pretty ballsy to me, add a little bit of turbo whine and anybody who knows will have reason enough to be scared  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
